From 6de6d41bd9d1dc2a078a2b6eed1f7709bd9da738 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:38:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0151: the GPU for 60 fps: asynchronous submits,
 write-combined GPU memory

Measured with CoreAnimation on Mesa (0149): ~15 fps, frames spent
waiting -- every submission ran to completion inside its call, every
mapped buffer was cleaned out of the CPU caches first (~3.5 ms), the
display cleaned each 1125x2436 frame (4.4 ms) the GPU had drawn, a
submission of 68 command buffers was refused (limit 64), and every
submission and frame copy printed a line.

- submissions return at once with their fence (ring space checked);
  WAIT_FENCE and GEM_CPU_PREP wait for it (2 s means the GPU hung and
  the service stops); a buffer given back while still in use is freed
  when its fence passes; up to 256 command buffers per submission.
- Mesa's buffers come from the unused DDR at 0x1_0000_0000 (1 GB, below
  xnu's 0x1_4000_0000), mapped write-combined: no cache maintenance.
  gpu_pool=0 goes back to 0149's cacheable buffers. GET_PARAM 0x1000
  tells libdrm which.
- the display skips the clean of a surface the GPU drew since its seed.
- no per-submission log lines once the service is up.
